-- title:
--   Torsion ideal on the origin chart is ([q]_F)
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a noetherian local ring that is adically complete for its maximal ideal, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $T$ with invertible discriminant. Let $F$ be a formal group over $T$ whose underlying two-variable power series is $W$'s fixed formal group law `W.formalGroupLawFixed`, and let $G$ be a relative group law on the projective Weierstrass model $\mathrm{Proj}$ of `projModelGradingCR W` over $\mathrm{Spec}\,T$, that is, a functorial group structure on $T$-scheme points. Assume (i) there exists an identification $ev$ of the points of $G$ over fields with the affine points of the base-changed curve, additive for $G$ and equivariant for Galois twists, and (ii) there exists a ring homomorphism $\chi : \mathrm{OriginChartRing}\ W \to T$ cutting out the unit section $G.one(\mathbb{1})$, with $\chi(\mathrm{xOverY}\ W)=\chi(\mathrm{zOverY}\ W)=0$. Let $q \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $\Phi : \mathrm{OriginChartRing}\ W \to T[[X]]$ be a ring homomorphism acting on degree-zero constants by $t \mapsto C(t)$ and with $\Phi(\mathrm{xOverY}\ W) = -X$, $\Phi(\mathrm{zOverY}\ W) = -\mathrm{W.formalW}$. Then the image under $\Phi$ composed with the global-sections isomorphism of the ideal, on the whole affine origin chart, obtained by pulling back the $q$-torsion ideal sheaf `torsionIdeal G q` (the kernel ideal sheaf of the first projection of the fibre product of $[q]_G$ and the unit section, followed by `toPullbackId`) along `originChartι W` followed by `toPullbackId`, is the principal ideal generated by `F.nthSeries q`, the $q$-fold iterate $[q]_F$ defined by $[0]_F=0$ and $[n+1]_F = F([n]_F, X)$.
--
--   This is the local form, at the origin chart of the projective Weierstrass model, of the statement that the ideal of $q$-torsion becomes the ideal generated by the multiplication-by-$q$ series $[q]_F$ of the formal group once pulled back along the formal parameter at the origin (as in Katz–Mazur 5.5). It feeds the Drinfeld-basis theory: it is used to factor $[q]_F$ through the origin parameters of a basis, and in the comparison of torsion divisors with basis divisors.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_DrinfeldGlobal_map_ideal_comap_torsionIdeal_eq_span_nthSeries.lean

